-- title:
--   Unit-box bounds for contributing twisted hyperbolic classes
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields, let $\nu_{Z_L}$ be a Haar measure on the idele units $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (with a Borel measurable structure), let $D$ be an `IdeleGaloisDescent`, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which are continuous and extend the action on $L$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (written via `Subgroup.zpowers`). Fix a finite set $S$ of finite places of $K$, a function $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$ and functions $\varphi_{S,v}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Let $H$ be a closed subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ consisting exactly of those $h$ whose off-diagonal entries $h_{10}, h_{01}$ vanish and for which $\sigma_D(h)h^{-1}$ is central, where $\sigma_D$ denotes the entrywise action of $D(\sigma)$; let $\mu_H$ be a right-invariant Haar measure on $H$. Let $\Delta \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be a set each of whose elements $t$ is diagonal with $\mathrm{N}_{K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \neq 1$, and such that distinct $t, t' \in \Delta$ have disjoint $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy classes modulo the centre, i.e. the sets $\{\delta : \exists g,\ t^{-1} g^{-1} \delta\, \sigma(g) \in Z(\mathrm{GL}_2(L))\}$ are disjoint. Then for every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ and every choice $w_v$ of a prime of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying under $v$, for each $v$, there are $A_0 \geq 0$ and real constants $c_S, c_\infty$, depending on none of the data below, with the following property. Let $\rho_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ for each $v$, let $\varphi$ be a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ one on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles, and suppose $\varphi$ is a semi-local factorisation relative to $S \cup T$ with archimedean factor $\varphi_a$, finite factor $\varphi_f$, and semi-local factor at $v$ equal to the characteristic function of the double coset $\mathcal{K}_v\, c_v(\rho_v)\, \mathcal{K}_v$ for $v \in T$ (where $\mathcal{K}_v$ is `semiLocalIntegralSet` and $c_v$ is the semi-local component of the local embedding of $\rho_v$) and to $\varphi_{S,v}$ for $v \notin T$. Let $t \in \Delta$, and suppose the iterated lower integral of $\bigl\|\varphi\bigl(q^{-1}\, t\, \sigma_D(z q)\bigr)\bigr\|$ over $z \in (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ with respect to $\nu_{Z_L}$ and over the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ by the $H$-orbit relation with respect to the quotient measure of the adelic Haar measure by $\mu_H$ (chosen representatives $q$, with $t$ and $z$ pushed into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ by the global-points and central-scalar maps) is non-zero. Then $r := \mathrm{N}_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11})$ satisfies: $r \neq 0$; $\|r\|_v = 1$ for every finite place $v \notin S \cup T$; $\bigl|\log\|r\|_v\bigr| \le A_0\bigl(1 + \log \mu'_v(\mathcal{K}_v c_v(\rho_v) \mathcal{K}_v)\bigr)$ for $v \in T$, where $\mu'_v$ is the semi-local Haar measure `semiLocalHaar`; $\bigl|\log\|r\|_v\bigr| \le c_S$ for $v \in S \setminus T$; and $|\log w(r)| \le c_\infty$ for every infinite place $w$ of $K$, all norms of $r$ being taken after mapping $r$ into the completion $K_v$.
--
--   This is the support estimate for the twisted orbital side of a trace formula: a $\sigma$-twisted hyperbolic class whose orbital term is not annihilated by the test function must have eigenvalue-ratio norm lying in an $(S \cup T)$-unit box whose size at $v \in T$ grows only logarithmically in the measure of the Hecke double coset. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_card_le_mul_prod_pow_log_measure_of_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_ne_zero`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_card_le_mul_prod_pow_log_measure_of_lintegral_orbital_doubleCoset_ne_zero) to bound the number of contributing classes.
